4 toreadasfollows:
5 329:16-g ContinuingMedicalEducationRequirement.
6 I. The board shall require each licensee to show proof at least at every biennial license renewal
7 that the licensee has completed 100 hours of approved continuing medical education program within
8 the preceding 2 years. For the purposes of this section, an approved continuing medical education
9 program is a program designed to continue the education of the licensee in current developments,
10 skills, procedures, or treatment in the licensee's field of practice, which has been certified by a
11 national, state, or county medical society or college or university. Each licensee shall submit a
12 continuing medical education report with copies of continuing medical education course certificates
13 earned by the licensee and other documents which establish that continuing medical education
14 courserequirementshavebeenmet,usingaformapprovedbytheboard.
15 II. As a condition for initial or continued licensure in New Hampshire, physicians,
16 nurse practitioners, and physician assistants shall be required to complete one hour of
17 education on child abuse and neglect as part of their mandatory continuing education
18 hours prescribed in paragraph I. This education shall be accredited for category 1
19 medical or nursing hours and recognized by the New Hampshire chapter of the American
20 AcademyofPediatricsasaddressingthetopicsofrecognition,reporting,andcollaboration
21 withthechildprotectionsystem.

